{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KYFiDwnuA5W48dSkGNByoG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\documentclass{article}\n2\t\n3\t% Load xcolor before corl_2026 (which loads color internally)\n4\t\\usepackage[table]{xcolor}\n5\t\\usepackage{corl_2026}\n6\t\n7\t\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n8\t\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n9\t\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\n10\t\\usepackage{booktabs}\n11\t\\usepackage{multirow}\n12\t\\usepackage{graphicx}\n13\t\\graphicspath{{../../artifacts/}}\n14\t\\usepackage{colortbl}\n15\t\\usepackage{caption}\n16\t\\usepackage{subcaption}\n17\t\\usepackage{array}\n18\t\\usepackage{enumitem}\n19\t\\usepackage{wrapfig}\n20\t\\usepackage{algorithm}\n21\t\\usepackage{algorithmic}\n22\t\n23\t% Custom commands\n24\t\\newcommand{\\dt}{\\mathrm{dt}}\n25\t\\newcommand{\\nve}{\\mathrm{nve}}\n26\t% SGS result values (018 seed 1: partial mitigation; seed 2: collapsed — 0/3 CIVO elimination)\n27\t\\newcommand{\\sgseval}{448.3}\n28\t\\newcommand{\\sgsnve}{1.66}\n29\t\\newcommand{\\sgsclaim}{reduced CIVO severity in one of two Walker seeds but eliminated it in neither (0/3 across environments)}\n30\t\\newcommand{\\ie}{\\textit{i.e.}}\n31\t\\newcommand{\\eg}{\\textit{e.g.}}\n32\t\\newcommand{\\cf}{\\textit{cf.}}\n33\t\\newcommand{\\etal}{\\textit{et al.}}\n34\t\n35\t\\title{Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in Imagination-Based RL:\\\\\n36\tA Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate DreamerV3}\n37\t\n38\t\\author{\n39\t  Anonymous Authors\n40\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62906dfe-36d5-453d-9d17-9efc70f5f581","uuid":"c6e127b5-b5a7-4740-9b7d-b7bc1be4e86b","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:34:48.197Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/docs/paper/main.tex","content":"\\documentclass{article}\n\n% Load xcolor before corl_2026 (which loads color internally)\n\\usepackage[table]{xcolor}\n\\usepackage{corl_2026}\n\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{multirow}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\graphicspath{{../../artifacts/}}\n\\usepackage{colortbl}\n\\usepackage{caption}\n\\usepackage{subcaption}\n\\usepackage{array}\n\\usepackage{enumitem}\n\\usepackage{wrapfig}\n\\usepackage{algorithm}\n\\usepackage{algorithmic}\n\n% Custom commands\n\\newcommand{\\dt}{\\mathrm{dt}}\n\\newcommand{\\nve}{\\mathrm{nve}}\n% SGS result values (018 seed 1: partial mitigation; seed 2: collapsed — 0/3 CIVO elimination)\n\\newcommand{\\sgseval}{448.3}\n\\newcommand{\\sgsnve}{1.66}\n\\newcommand{\\sgsclaim}{reduced CIVO severity in one of two Walker seeds but eliminated it in neither (0/3 across environments)}\n\\newcommand{\\ie}{\\textit{i.e.}}\n\\newcommand{\\eg}{\\textit{e.g.}}\n\\newcommand{\\cf}{\\textit{cf.}}\n\\newcommand{\\etal}{\\textit{et al.}}\n\n\\title{Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in Imagination-Based RL:\\\\\nA Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate DreamerV3}\n\n\\author{\n  Anonymous Authors\n}","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":77}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Pkjc175R4epkUvikeLqFGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good picture. I'll use the CoRL template style and write a comprehensive paper. Let me construct the full LaTeX source. I need to copy the corl_2026.sty to the target directory or reference it properly.\n\nLet me write the paper. I'll need to:\n1. Copy the sty file to the target directory\n2. Write paper.tex with full content\n3. Create a minimal bib file\n4. Compile\n\nLet me structure the paper carefully based on all the experiment data.\n\nKey experiments to cover with tables:\n1. Cross-environment CIVO severity (Walker, Cheetah, Cartpole, Hopper) - C1/C2\n\n\n2. The 2×2 intervention matrix showing different dt_emb configurations - C2\n3. NVE threshold classification results - C2\n4. RSSM fidelity measurements - C2 mechanism\n5. Cross-seed NVE comparison - C2\n6. No-dt-emb causal control results - C2\n7. dt_emb value suppression under unexposed conditions - C3\n8. dt=1 imagination collapse summary - C6\n9. Dual mechanism analysis and pathway collapse comparison - C6\n10. Embedding removal across environments - C7\n11. SGS failure patterns - C7\n12. TCN dose-response curves - C8\n13. TCN per-seed Walker results - C8\n14. Cheetah configuration comparison - C3\n15. Cosine similarity trajectories - C2 mechanism\n\nNow I'm thinking through how to structure this into a coherent paper. I'll start with the abstract covering the CIVO finding across 31+ configurations and 4 environments, then highlight the SGS failure and TCN success. The introduction should establish why temporal abstraction matters and what puzzle we're solving. Background covers DreamerV3, temporal abstraction mechanisms, and value overestimation issues in model-based RL. For methodology, I need to detail the DreamerV3 modifications and experimental setup.\n\nThe diagnostic results section will be the core, organized by finding: variable-rate imagination consistently hurts performance across environments, the trained dt_embedding acts as a CIVO trigger with supporting ablation matrices and threshold analysis, RSSM fidelity gaps explain the mechanism through cosine similarity, and untrained embeddings suppress value drift. I'll include tables for cross-environment comparisons, ablation matrices, and seed-level analysis throughout.\n\nThen I'm moving into the exploratory forward-pass intervention work with TCN design and dose-response curves from the Walker Walk experiments, followed by cross-environment challenges and limitations. The discussion will compare MPC versus imagination approaches and map out the intervention difficulty gradient before concluding. Now I'm mapping out the remaining experiments to their corresponding sections—additional Walker seeds for the imaginary mitigation analysis, the full Cheetah Run suite across baseline and ablation conditions, and then several analysis sections covering RSSM prediction quality, actor entropy, value distributions, embedding similarity, and NVE thresholds. Now I'm ready to write out the full paper using the CoRL template, making sure to copy over the style file and place each experiment in its designated section.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":67873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62906dfe-36d5-453d-9d17-9efc70f5f581","uuid":"ac29c692-fc0c-444c-8997-b13631af9783"}
